Key Computer Hardware Components

    The Role of the Motherboard
  
    - Facilitates communication between all components
    - Houses CPU socket, RAM slots, expansion slots and storage connectors
    - Several types
      - ATX (Advanced Technoligy eXtended)
      - MicroATX
      - Mini-ITX
    - Must match CPU socket and RAM type
    - Choose based on the number of PCIe (Peripheral Component Interconnect express) slots required
  
   Central Processing Unit (CPU)
  
    - Executes instructions from software and hardware
    - Speed measured in hertz (GHz)
      - Instructions/Second = Clock Frequency x IPC (Instructions Per Cycle)
      - 1 Cycle/Second = 1Hz
      - Today the average CPU does at 3GHz tens of billions Instructions
    - Key features - cores and threads, clock speed, cache memory
    - Ensure compatibility with the motherboard socket type
    - Check power and cooling requirements
  
  Random Access Memory (RAM)
  
    - Temporarily stores data for active applications
    - Faster than storage devices but volatile (erased on shutdown)
    - Types
      - DIMM (Dual In-line Memory Module)
      - SODIMM (Small Outline Dual In-line Memory Module) for laptops
      - DDR (Double Data Rate)
      - ECC (Error Correction Code)
      - non-ECC (non Error Correction Code)
    - Must match motherboard specifications
    - More RAM improves multitaksing and speed
  
  Storage Devices - HDD vs. SSD
  
    - M.2 NVMe (Non Volatile Memory) SSDs - high-speed storage directly connected to the motherboard      fastest
    - Solid-state drives (SSDs) - faster, more durable, but more expensive                                fast
    - Hard disk drives (HDDs) - magnetic storage, slower, but cost-effective for large capacity           slow
  
  Power Supply Units (PSUs)
  
    - Converts electrical power from the wall outlet into usable power for components
    - Measured in watts (W) and efficiency rating (80 Plus standard)
  
  Cooling Systems
  
    - Air cooling
    - Liquid cooling
    - Thermal paste
  
  Expansion Cards
  
    - Graphics precessing unit (GPU)
    - Network interface card (NIC)
    - Sound card
  
  Peripherals
  
    - Monitors, keyboards, mice, printers, and external storage, webcam, ...
    - Input/output devices for user interaction and functionality


